    "body": "\nProblem:\nWhen starting Nvim with both `--clean` and `--noplugin` (in either\norder), `--noplugin` is silently ignored and built-in runtime plugins\nare loaded anyway. `command_line_scan()` sets `p_lpl = false` for\n`--noplugin`, and `--clean` sets `params.use_vimrc = \"NONE\"` and\n`params.clean = true`, which later overwrites `p_lpl` back to `true` via\n`p_lpl = vimrc_none ? params.clean : p_lpl`.\n\nSolution:\nOnly reset `p_lpl = false` when `vimrc_none && !params.clean`,\npreserving `p_lpl = false` if `--noplugin` was passed.\n\nCloses #42361\n\nAI-assisted\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-16T10:00:29Z",
